Workstream ID: discovery-atlas
Title: Evidence-based discovery collection and final tutorial chapter
Status: IN_REVIEW
Milestone: Make useful recorded practice rewarding without inventing career progress
Dependencies: tracker-foundation, appearance-and-identity, versioned-roadmaps, tutorial-and-help
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/9
Purpose: Add an optional, visually rich discovery collection derived from existing
  evidence and recall records. Preserve every existing workflow and teach the
  addition in a final isolated tutorial chapter.

Tasks:
  [x] Derive a finite collection from meaningful saved work, not clicks or timers.
  [x] Deduplicate verified roadmap lineage and exclude future calendar days.
  [x] Add responsive themed visual exploration, provenance and useful next actions.
  [x] Preserve normal backups, encrypted journal, criteria and tutorial isolation.
  [x] Append hands-on tutorial lessons and focused guide/architecture references.
  [x] Replace the rejected character presentation after game-progression research.
  [x] Give every collection level distinct artwork, rewards and a real level-up sequence.
  [x] Add the requested freely rotatable minimal PS1-style 3D avatar with cumulative equipment.
  [x] Bound geometry, draw calls and render resolution; verify idle/offscreen suspension and disposal.
  [x] Update the final tutorial and qualify revised motion, accessibility and both themes.
  [x] Replace the flat backdrop with an orbitable, movable isometric 3D diorama.
  [x] Requalify all chapter scenes, camera controls, tutorial and graphics budgets.
  [ ] Synchronize this workstream, publish authorized commits and verify Pages.

Acceptance criteria:
  Collection recognizes recorded work, not independently assessed ability.
  Repeated records cannot farm distinct-checkpoint or same-day milestones.
  Unrelated roadmap editions stay distinct; verified append lineage counts once.
  Existing workspace schema, storage keys, evidence gates and exports coexist.
  No new network service, automatic publication, leaderboard or punitive expiry.
  Collection visuals communicate actual data; avatar renders only on interaction,
    resize, equipment changes or a bounded level-up, never an idle animation loop.
  The original low-poly 3D avatar supports mouse, touch and keyboard orbit/zoom.
  Real chapter terrain shares the camera; pan mode works with mouse and touch,
    and reset restores the isometric angle, target, zoom and rotation mode.
  Earned equipment is added cumulatively, including visible back/side details.
  Use the existing Three.js dependency without textures, shadows or postprocessing.
  Record actual performance evidence and limits; do not promise zero GPU cost.
  Seven fictional character levels reflect discoveries, not measured capability.
  Every level has a distinct visual payoff, not the same idle animation recoloured.
  Level-ups explain the threshold crossed and what changed; replay awards nothing.
  Automatic motion ends and can be skipped; reduced motion keeps effects still,
    while deliberate manual camera controls remain available.
  Keyboard, mobile, light/dark and reduced-motion behavior are exercised.
  New tutorial content is appended; every earlier lesson remains available.
  Synthetic examples never enter the real workspace or public progress journal.
  Technical completion, user acceptance and actual deployment remain separate.

Completion evidence:
  Current isometric diorama: seven real batched chapter environments, shared
    orthographic camera, deliberate orbit/pan/zoom, cumulative earned equipment.
  Current TypeScript/689 unit cases and production build pass; the unchanged
    tracking runtime retains its 22-case qualification.
  Final 24-case local browser gate passes: all collection/avatar cases, complete
    170-step tour at 1440px, final chapter at 320px, both backup workflows and
    tutorial isolation from the actual encrypted journal.
  Native mouse/keyboard orbit/pan, touch drag/pinch/pan, zoom/reset, chapter replay,
    every crossed reward, reduced motion and unavailable-WebGL messaging pass.
  Seven chapter/reveal sheets, four real 3D angles and dark/light phone views
    were inspected. A focused seven-chapter rerun additionally confirms actual
    new WebGL paints before frozen-clock reveal captures. No approval is inferred.
  Level-seven terrain plus equipment: 1,292 triangles, eight draw calls,
    332x248 buffer; all seven scenes fit the tested geometry/pixel budgets.
  The local Edge probe observed zero extra frames over one second idle and
    one second offscreen. Fifty-two warm CPU render-submission samples had
    median 0.4ms and p95 0.5ms; this excludes GPU completion/startup and is not
    an actual-phone or universal-FPS guarantee.
  The new reset lesson exposed a real asynchronous observation race: camera
    reset completed but the coach had checked before its WebGL frame. Observing
    the relevant discovery attributes fixes the gate without timers or relaxed tests.
  Lazy loading avoids avatar renderer requests from ordinary non-3D routes.
  Earlier avatar-only evidence: 688 units, 169-step tour, 24 browser cases,
    1,028 triangles/eight calls/384x216; superseded by the full-diorama figures.
  Complete evidence, source limits and publication status:
    docs/tracking/2026-11-09-discovery-delivery.md; docs/DISCOVERY-DESIGN.md.
  Prototype source abcbabdeb71bb8788f36adb8efdbdc377edb734d was committed/pushed.
  Its character presentation was rejected; the qualification above supersedes it.
  Prototype TypeScript and 685 unit cases passed; tracking suite: 22 passed.
  The earlier 56-case affected browser gate passed, including the complete tour
  at 1440/390/320px and normal/encrypted backup coexistence.
  The prototype character follow-up added two lessons (164 total, 29 chapters). Its
  13-case browser pass covers all twelve discovery cases and the complete 164-step
  tour at 1440px; the appended chapter also passes at 320px.
  Actual dark/light desktop/tablet/phone captures and final character form reviewed.
  Normal evidence recording stays operable while a level-up notice is visible.
  Full evidence and limits: docs/tracking/2026-11-09-discovery-delivery.md.
  An accidentally nested browser-test registration was caught and moved to
  module scope; no product validation or assertions were weakened.
  Human acceptance: original character presentation rejected; revised acceptance unrecorded.
  Superseded Pages run 42598017993 was intentionally cancelled before deployment.
  Publication: a corrective commit, push and exact-source Pages verification remain authorized.
  Prior local tracking adoption files remain preserved for reviewed publication.

